From 388242aaa4f3b2a34297a2bd63308de92f4cd5da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_sched_tc_fixed <>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:27:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apps/examples/testcase: add starvation invariant monitor and
 SMP scenario family

Phase 2 of the scenario test rollout.  Where each round-robin scenario
targets one known mechanism, this adds a detector for the property those
mechanisms exist to uphold: no runnable task is passed over indefinitely.
It holds regardless of which part of the scheduler is at fault, so it
catches starvation defects that no specific scenario was written for.

stc_sched_monitor is a background sampler.  It reads scheduler state every
10 ms through the OS API test driver, which calls sched_foreach on its
behalf, and measures for each task how long it stays continuously ready to
run without being given a CPU.  Exceeding the grace period raises one
violation per episode rather than one per sample, so a permanently starved
task contributes a stable count instead of one proportional to how long the
scenario happened to run.  The walk holds a critical section, so the
sampling callback only copies three fields per task and every decision is
made afterwards.

The monitor opens the test driver itself rather than reusing the descriptor
held by the task that starts it.  task_create() gives the new task its own
task group, and with CONFIG_FDCLONE_STDIO only descriptors 0, 1 and 2 are
cloned into it, so a borrowed descriptor is simply not valid there; see
NFDS_TOCLONE in group_setuptaskfiles.c.  Getting this wrong makes every
ioctl fail and the violation count stay at zero for want of any data, which
is why an open failure is now recorded and reported rather than ignored.

Two limitations are recorded in the header because both are load bearing.
The monitor perturbs what it observes: each time it blocks,
sched_removereadytorun() runs on its CPU and pulls a waiting task in, which
is rotation supplied by the observer at a rate close to CONFIG_RR_INTERVAL.
For the same reason it is blind on its own CPU.  It is therefore not wired
into the round-robin scenarios, whose oracle is a share of CPU time, and is
used only where it is the instrument rather than a bystander.

stc_sched_smp adds SCN-SMP-01, which runs the monitor over an oversubscribed
equal priority workload and asserts no violations, having first asserted the
monitor actually sampled so that a zero count cannot be vacuous.

Both the SMP and non-SMP compilation paths are warning free under -Wall
-Wextra.
